Z||000000||Dan010||11-03-2001||08:31 PM||||Was reading in OGREs cave, found a tread about v6 auxiliary fan/engine bay fan, does all v6 have this? if so where is it located?<BR>I have a 86 2.8, been working on it, looking at the haynes book but have not seen any thing about this.<BR>THanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-03-2001||08:45 PM||||The fan lives under the right side of the trunk liner.  Look in your engine compartment and see if you have a couple of tubes pointed at the alternator and the ignition coil areas of the engine.  As far as I know, all 85-87 V-6's had the fans.  They dropped it for the 88's.  Haynes doesn't cover the blower (along with a lot of other stuff).<BR>It's also possible that a previous owner removed the system if you don't see any signs of it.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan010||11-03-2001||09:37 PM||||I found the tubes and finally the fan, it was disconnected, not sure if it works, when and or how does it get turned on? is there a test for this like the rad. fan?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan010||11-03-2001||09:53 PM||||jumped the fan motor, moter works, good sign!!  now is this a temperature switch or something else to turn this thing on??||||reg||1
